    "steps": [
        {
            "id": "hall-sensor",
            "title": "Hall Sensor Issue (2023 Models)",
            "content": "",
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "id": "hs-severity",
                    "type": "callout",
                    "variant": "danger",
                    "title": "Critical Hardware Defect",
                    "content": "<p>This is a known design flaw in 2023 OMEN models affecting the Hall Sensor ribbon cable placement. This issue can cause significant usability problems.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "id": "hs-desc",
                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "<p><strong>Description:</strong> A design flaw in 2023 models affects the Hall Sensor ribbon cable placement, often causing black screen issues or sleep mode problems. The Hall Sensor is responsible for detecting when the laptop lid is opened or closed.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "id": "hs-symptoms-title",
                    "type": "heading",
                    "level": 3,
                    "content": "Symptoms"
                },
                {
                    "id": "hs-symptoms",
                    "type": "list",
                    "content": {
                        "style": "unordered",
                        "items": [
                            "Black screen upon opening lid",
                            "Laptop failing to wake from sleep",
                            "Intermittent display issues when adjusting lid angle",
                            "Random sleep triggers while laptop is open"
                        ]
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "hs-solutions-title",
                    "type": "heading",
                    "level": 3,
                    "content": "Solutions"
                },
                {
                    "id": "hs-solutions",
                    "type": "list",
                    "content": {
                        "style": "ordered",
                        "items": [
                            "<strong>Temporary Fix:</strong> Disconnect the Hall Sensor ribbon cable (Note: This disables the lid close sleep function)",
                            "<strong>Warranty Repair:</strong> Contact HP Support for motherboard replacement if under warranty",
                            "<strong>Professional Repair:</strong> Seek professional repair service to reroute or replace the ribbon cable"
                        ]
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "hs-note",
                    "type": "callout",
                    "variant": "info",
                    "title": "Affected Models",
                    "content": "<p>Primarily affects OMEN 16/17 laptops manufactured in 2023. Check your serial number with HP Support to confirm if your model is affected.</p>"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "battery-drain",
            "title": "High Battery Drain",
            "content": "",
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "id": "bd-severity",
                    "type": "callout",
                    "variant": "warning",
                    "title": "High Severity Issue",
                    "content": "<p>This issue significantly impacts laptop portability and may indicate background processes or firmware problems.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "id": "bd-desc",
                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "<p><strong>Description:</strong> Excessive battery consumption even during light usage or sleep mode. Users report battery depleting much faster than expected, even when not performing intensive tasks.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "id": "bd-symptoms-title",
                    "type": "heading",
                    "level": 3,
                    "content": "Symptoms"
                },
                {
                    "id": "bd-symptoms",
                    "type": "list",
                    "content": {
                        "style": "unordered",
                        "items": [
                            "Battery depleting rapidly in standby mode",
                            "Low battery life during non-gaming tasks (web browsing, documents)",
                            "Laptop warm to touch while in sleep mode",
                            "Battery percentage dropping overnight even when 'sleeping'"
                        ]
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "bd-solutions-title",
                    "type": "heading",
                    "level": 3,
                    "content": "Solutions"
                },
                {
                    "id": "bd-solutions",
                    "type": "list",
                    "content": {
                        "style": "ordered",
                        "items": [
                            "<strong>Update BIOS:</strong> Download and install the latest BIOS from HP Support website",
                            "<strong>Disable Fast Startup:</strong> Go to Control Panel → Power Options → Choose what the power buttons do → Disable 'Turn on fast startup'",
                            "<strong>Check Background Apps:</strong> Open Task Manager and identify apps with high power usage",
                            "<strong>Battery Calibration:</strong> Use HP Support Assistant to run battery diagnostics and calibration"
                        ]
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "bd-code",
                    "type": "code",
                    "language": "powershell",
                    "filename": "Check Battery Health",
                    "content": "# Run in PowerShell as Administrator\npowercfg /batteryreport /output \"C:\\battery-report.html\"\n\n# Open the report\nStart-Process \"C:\\battery-report.html\""
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "driver-power-state",
            "title": "Driver Power State Failure (BSOD)",
            "content": "",
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "id": "dps-severity",
                    "type": "callout",
                    "variant": "warning",
                    "title": "Medium Severity - System Stability",
                    "content": "<p>Blue Screen crashes can cause data loss. Save work frequently until this issue is resolved.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "id": "dps-desc",
                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "<p><strong>Description:</strong> Blue Screen of Death (BSOD) with error code <code>DRIVER_POWER_STATE_FAILURE</code>. This error is usually triggered during power management transitions, such as waking from sleep or switching between power states.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "id": "dps-symptoms-title",
                    "type": "heading",
                    "level": 3,
                    "content": "Symptoms"
                },
                {
                    "id": "dps-symptoms",
                    "type": "list",
                    "content": {
                        "style": "unordered",
                        "items": [
                            "Blue Screen of Death (BSOD) with stop code DRIVER_POWER_STATE_FAILURE",
                            "System freeze during sleep/wake cycles",
                            "Crash when switching between battery and AC power",
                            "Random restarts when changing power plans"
                        ]
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "dps-solutions-title",
                    "type": "heading",
                    "level": 3,
                    "content": "Solutions"
                },
                {
                    "id": "dps-grid",
                    "type": "grid",
                    "columns": 2,
                    "children": [
                        {
                            "id": "dps-col1",
                            "type": "column",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "id": "dps-basic-title",
                                    "type": "heading",
                                    "level": 4,
                                    "content": "Basic Fixes"
                                },
                                {
                                    "id": "dps-basic",
                                    "type": "list",
                                    "content": {
                                        "style": "ordered",
                                        "items": [
                                            "Update graphics drivers (NVIDIA/AMD)",
                                            "Update chipset drivers from HP",
                                            "Set Power Plan to High Performance",
                                            "Run Windows Update"
                                        ]
                                    }
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "dps-col2",
                            "type": "column",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "id": "dps-advanced-title",
                                    "type": "heading",
                                    "level": 4,
                                    "content": "Advanced Fixes"
                                },
                                {
                                    "id": "dps-advanced",
                                    "type": "list",
                                    "content": {
                                        "style": "ordered",
                                        "items": [
                                            "Disable Link State Power Management",
                                            "Run Windows Driver Verifier",
                                            "Check Event Viewer for faulting driver",
                                            "Perform clean driver install"
                                        ]
                                    }
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "id": "dps-disable-lspm",
                    "type": "callout",
                    "variant": "info",
                    "title": "Disable Link State Power Management",
                    "content": "<p>Go to <strong>Control Panel → Power Options → Change plan settings → Change advanced power settings → PCI Express → Link State Power Management</strong> and set to <strong>Off</strong>.</p>"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "vbios-flashing",
            "title": "vBIOS Flashing (Advanced)",
            "content": "",
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "id": "vbios-warn",
                    "type": "callout",
                    "variant": "danger",
                    "title": "Warning - Experienced Users Only",
                    "content": "<p>vBIOS flashing <strong>WILL void your warranty</strong>, can cause serious GPU/VRM overheating, can break IO ports, and potentially brick your laptop. Proceed only if you understand the risks.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "id": "vbios-disclaimer",
                    "type": "callout",
                    "variant": "danger",
                    "title": "DISCLAIMER - Proceed at Your Own Risk",
                    "content": "<p><strong>By proceeding with vBIOS flashing, you acknowledge that you do so ENTIRELY AT YOUR OWN RISK.</strong> The author(s) of this documentation are <strong>NOT RESPONSIBLE</strong> for any damage, bricked devices, voided warranties, overheating, fires, or any other consequences. This is an advanced modification intended for experienced users only. If you are unsure, <strong>DO NOT proceed</strong>.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "id": "vbios-text",
                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "<p>Some OMEN laptops can have their GPU vBIOS flashed for higher power limits:</p>"
                },
                {
                    "id": "vbios-table",
                    "type": "table",
                    "content": {
                        "headers": ["GPU Model", "Can Flash?", "Max Power", "Notes"],
                        "rows": [
                            ["RTX 2060", "Yes", "Up to 115W", "Use 115W vBIOS from community"],
                            ["RTX 3060", "Yes", "Up to 130W", "Requires 230W power brick"],
                            ["RTX 3070", "No", "N/A", "Board IDs differ between 100W and 140W models"]
                        ]
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "vbios-rtx2060-h",
                    "type": "heading",
                    "level": 3,
                    "content": "RTX 2060 Flash Guide (115W)"
                },
                {
                    "id": "vbios-rtx2060-steps",
                    "type": "list",
                    "content": {
                        "style": "ordered",
                        "items": [
                            "Download the 115W vBIOS file and nvflash tool from the OMEN Discord #advanced-mods channel",
                            "Extract contents to C:\\ drive",
                            "Open CMD as Administrator",
                            "Run the backup and flash commands below",
                            "Answer YES to both prompts when asked",
                            "Restart when complete"
                        ]
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "vbios-rtx2060-code",
                    "type": "code",
                    "language": "batch",
                    "filename": "RTX 2060 Flash Commands",
                    "code": "cd C:\\\n\n:: Disable GPU protection\nnvflash --protectoff\n\n:: IMPORTANT: Backup your original vBIOS first!\nnvflash --save original-vbios.rom\n\n:: Flash the 115W vBIOS (replace with your filename)\nnvflash -6 225910.rom"
                },
                {
                    "id": "vbios-rtx3060-h",
                    "type": "heading",
                    "level": 3,
                    "content": "RTX 3060 Flash Guide (130W)"
                },
                {
                    "id": "vbios-rtx3060-warn",
                    "type": "callout",
                    "variant": "warning",
                    "title": "Additional Requirements",
                    "content": "<p><strong>Before flashing RTX 3060 to 130W:</strong><br/>• Repaste your laptop - this WILL increase heat significantly<br/>• Buy a 230W power brick (OMEN 16 brick or Elitebook HSTNN-LA12 with 5.5mm→7.4mm adapter)<br/>• Stock 200W brick will cause throttling when battery drops below 50%<br/>• Short 1-2 hour sessions work on stock brick</p>"
                },
                {
                    "id": "vbios-rtx3060-code",
                    "type": "code",
                    "language": "batch",
                    "filename": "RTX 3060 Flash Commands",
                    "code": "cd C:\\\n\n:: Backup your original vBIOS first!\nnvflash64 --protectoff\nnvflash64 --save original-vbios.rom\n\n:: Flash the 130W vBIOS\nnvflash64 -6 130w.rom"
                },
                {
                    "id": "vbios-restore-h",
                    "type": "heading",
                    "level": 3,
                    "content": "Restoring Original vBIOS"
                },
                {
                    "id": "vbios-restore",
                    "type": "code",
                    "language": "batch",
                    "filename": "Restore Original vBIOS",
                    "code": "cd C:\\\nnvflash64 -6 original-vbios.rom"
                },
                {
                    "id": "vbios-note",
                    "type": "callout",
                    "variant": "info",
                    "title": "Get vBIOS Files",
                    "content": "<p>The vBIOS files and nvflash tool are available in the OMEN Discord community's #advanced-mods channel. Join via the Discord link in the sidebar.</p>"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "windows11-issues",
            "title": "Windows 11 Compatibility",
            "content": "",
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "id": "w11-text",
                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "<p>Windows 11 can cause various issues on OMEN laptops due to driver compatibility:</p>"
                },
                {
                    "id": "w11-list",
                    "type": "list",
                    "content": {
                        "style": "unordered",
                        "items": [
                            "<strong>Battery life:</strong> Significantly worse than Windows 10 due to driver issues",
                            "<strong>VBS (Virtualization Based Security):</strong> Causes errors in OGH, XTU, and ThrottleStop",
                            "<strong>AMD stuttering:</strong> More common on Windows 11",
                            "<strong>Sleep/Wake issues:</strong> May be more frequent"
                        ]
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "w11-tip",
                    "type": "callout",
                    "variant": "info",
                    "title": "Should You Upgrade?",
                    "content": "<p>If your OMEN is running well on Windows 10, consider staying on Win10 unless you specifically need Windows 11 features. HP drivers have better compatibility with Windows 10.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "id": "w11-videos",
                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "<p>Videos to help you decide on Windows 11:</p>"
                },
                {
                    "id": "w11-video1",
                    "type": "code",
                    "language": "url",
                    "code": "https://youtu.be/hJ0dLimSiNM"
                },
                {
                    "id": "w11-video2",
                    "type": "code",
                    "language": "url",
                    "code": "https://youtu.be/zt3zvY7KzYs"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "report-issues",
            "title": "Reporting New Issues",
            "content": "",
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "id": "ri-intro",
                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "<p>If you've encountered an issue not listed here, please help the community by reporting it. Your contribution helps other OMEN users solve similar problems.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "id": "ri-how",
                    "type": "heading",
                    "level": 3,
                    "content": "How to Report"
                },
                {
                    "id": "ri-steps",
                    "type": "list",
                    "content": {
                        "style": "ordered",
                        "items": [
                            "Join the OMEN Discord community (link in sidebar)",
                            "Describe your issue with as much detail as possible",
                            "Include your laptop model, BIOS version, and Windows version",
                            "Share any error codes or screenshots",
                            "Mention any solutions you've already tried"
                        ]
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "ri-template",
                    "type": "code",
                    "language": "markdown",
                    "filename": "Issue Report Template",
                    "code": "## Issue Report\n\n**Model:** OMEN 16 (2023)\n**BIOS Version:** F.12\n**Windows Version:** Windows 11 23H2\n\n**Problem:**\n[Describe the issue]\n\n**Steps to Reproduce:**\n1. [Step 1]\n2. [Step 2]\n\n**Expected Behavior:**\n[What should happen]\n\n**Actual Behavior:**\n[What actually happens]\n\n**Solutions Tried:**\n- [Solution 1]\n- [Solution 2]"
                }
            ]
        },
